      template: "You extract structured business knowledge graph entities from Aviators catalog documents.\nReturn ONLY valid JSON. No markdown.\n\nEntity types allowed:\n- offering: Globant engagement models (e.g. T&M, Fixed Price, Managed Services).\n- technology: Specific technology, framework, platform, or tool used (e.g. React, AWS, Salesforce).\n- outcome: Business result achieved (e.g. 40% cost reduction, improved NPS).\n- theme: Strategic topic or domain (e.g. digital transformation, AI, cloud migration).\n- challenge: Problem or pain-point faced by the client before the engagement (e.g. legacy system debt, high churn rate). Use field \"label\" for a concise description (max 80 chars).\n- metric: A quantified KPI or result (e.g. \"30% faster deployments\"). Use field \"label\" for the metric name, \"value\" for the numeric/textual measure, and \"unit\" (optional) for the unit (e.g. \"%\", \"ms\", \"x\").\n- globant_product: Named Globant product, studio, or capability (e.g. AI Pods, Globant Create, Nearshore, GeneXus). Do NOT use for generic technologies.\n\nRelation types allowed (from content node to entity):\n- delivers → offering\n- uses_technology → technology\n- achieved → outcome\n- addresses_theme → theme\n- had_challenge → challenge\n- measured_by → metric\n- leveraged_product → globant_product\n\n{{offeringRule}}\n\nJSON schema:\n{\"entities\":[{\"type\":\"<type>\",\"label\":\"<label>\",\"value\":\"<optional>\",\"unit\":\"<optional>\",\"category\":\"<optional for globant_product>\"},...],\"relations\":[{\"relation\":\"<relation_type>\",\"entity_index\":<0-based index in entities array>,\"confidence\":<0.5-1.0>},...],\"slide_types\":[\"<slide_type>\",...]}.\n\nMax {{maxEntities}} entities and {{maxRelations}} relations.\n\nSlide type classification:\nAlso return a top-level \"slide_types\" array identifying which presentation slide sections this content is best suited for. Choose only from:\n- executive_summary: overviews, introductions, company profiles.\n- challenge_diagnosis: problem statements, pain-points, client needs.\n- proposed_solution: how Globant addresses the problem, methodology, architecture.\n- success_case: past project results, client success stories, case studies.\n- team_credentials: team profiles, certifications, org structure.\n- commercial_proposal: pricing, timeline, engagement model, commercial terms.\nInclude only the types clearly supported by the document content. Omit if uncertain.",
